  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The loop: submit -> poll the SERVICE -> land back in BRONZE",
      "items": [
        "4-6: seam submits (build_adapter(name) names the provider); async job OUTSIDE Dagster; Dagster polls THE SERVICE: GET /jobs/{id} -> pending/processing/completed/failed until is_terminal (max_polls) - NO ledger (ADR-0013): handle + loop live in the Dagster run, never a queue",
        "retrieve(handle) lands responses VERBATIM in bronze_enrichment_raw (append-only, immutable) - the paid + stochastic part ENDS there",
        "7: conform re-reads bronze with ZERO API calls - a schema change is a REPLAY, never a re-bill"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What replaces the queue",
      "items": [
        "Retry: batch_items.scheduled_for -> NEW dynamic partition key (enrichment_submitted / enrichment_harvested); failures: dead_letter -> BLOCKING landed MINUS conformed anti-join",
        "ops.sqlite keeps media_cache, media_metadata, creators, profiles, creator_merges, prompt_registry; GOLD marts: gold_post_enrichment, gold_creator_performance, gold_content_shape_performance, gold_top_posts. Dagster owns ALL data assets in ONE boundary; the inference service and ops.sqlite sit OUTSIDE it"
      ]
    }
